@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# FinFlowTrack Blog — Editor & Developer Guide
+
+The blog lives in the repo. Adding a Markdown file and pushing to GitHub is the
+entire publishing workflow — Vercel rebuilds automatically and the article goes
+live at `https://finflowtrack.com/blog/<slug>`.
+
+## How to create an article
+
+1. Add a new file: `content/blog/my-new-article.md`
+2. Fill in the frontmatter block (see below).
+3. Write the body in Markdown underneath the closing `---`.
+4. Commit and push.
+
+```bash
+git add content/blog/my-new-article.md
+git commit -m "Add new blog article"
+git push
+```
+
+That's it — no route files, no registries, no database records to touch.
+
+## Required frontmatter
+
+```yaml
+---
+title: "How to Create an Invoice"
+description: "A short summary shown on cards and used as the meta description."
+slug: "how-to-create-an-invoice"
+author: "FinFlowTrack Editorial Team"
+publishedAt: "2026-08-11"
+category: "invoicing-payments"
+tags:
+  - invoicing
+  - small business
+featured: false
+draft: false
+---
+```
+
+| Field | Required | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `title` | yes | |
+| `description` | yes | Used for the excerpt and `<meta name="description">` |
+| `slug` | yes | Lowercase kebab-case. Should match the filename, but the frontmatter value wins if they differ. |
+| `author` | yes | |
+| `publishedAt` | yes | ISO date, e.g. `2026-08-11` |
+| `category` | yes | Must match a slug in `src/lib/blog/categories.ts` — the build fails with a clear error otherwise |
+| `updatedAt` | no | Defaults to `publishedAt` |
+| `tags` | no | Array of strings, used for related-article matching |
+| `featured` | no | One featured article is shown at the top of `/blog` |
+| `coverImage` | no | Path under `public/blog/images/...` or an absolute URL |
+| `readingTime` | no | Manual override in minutes; otherwise computed from word count |
+| `canonicalUrl` | no | Only set this if the article's canonical home is elsewhere |
+| `draft` | no | `true` hides it from the index, sitemap, RSS, and related posts (see below) |
+
+The build fails loudly (naming the exact file and field) if a required field
+is missing, a date is invalid, the category doesn't exist, or two articles
+share a slug — so a bad article can't silently ship with broken SEO.
+
+## Adding images
+
+Put images under `public/blog/images/` and reference them as `/blog/images/your-image.jpg`
+in `coverImage` or inline in the Markdown body (`![alt text](/blog/images/foo.jpg)`).
+
+## Creating a draft
+
+Set `draft: true`. Draft articles:
+- 404 if visited directly
+- are excluded from `/blog`, the sitemap, the RSS feed, and related-article suggestions
+
+Flip it to `false` (or remove the line) when ready to publish.
+
+## Updating an article
+
+Edit the file and bump `updatedAt`. The article page shows an "Updated" date
+separately from "Published" whenever the two differ.
+
+## How URLs are generated
+
+The slug (frontmatter `slug`, falling back to the filename) becomes the path:
+`content/blog/my-article.md` → `/blog/my-article`. No route file or registry
+entry is needed per article — `src/lib/blog/posts.ts` discovers every file in
+`content/blog/*.md` at build time via `import.meta.glob`.
+
+## Categories
+
+Categories are a small, fixed list in `src/lib/blog/categories.ts` (icon, name,
+description). To add a new category, add an entry there first, then reference
+its `slug` in article frontmatter.
+
+## Table of contents & reading time
+
+Both are automatic — generated from the article's H2/H3 headings and word
+count respectively. No manual maintenance required.
